# React Native Security Rules

- No hardcoded secrets in JS, app config, native config, or public EAS env.
- Tokens and refresh secrets live in expo-secure-store.
- AsyncStorage is only for non-sensitive preferences.
- Validate deep links, push payloads, clipboard content, QR scans, and native intents.
- Allowlist external URL schemes/hosts.
- Production traffic uses HTTPS/WSS only.
- Prefer Expo SDK modules; run the dependency gate and Expo Doctor before native dependencies.
